# Lint rules — clause

## Status

`mock/crates/` is empty at seed. Custom per-crate lints for the
Clause compiler and runtime are **deferred to post-R1–R4** (the first
four design rounds that decide the crate split). Once crates exist,
this skill grows a full lint table. Until then, only built-in lints
run.

## Severity system

Every lint has three independent gate levels — what happens on
commit, on build, and on push. Four levels per gate: **error**
(blocks), **warn** (reported, no block), **info** (informational),
**off** (silent).

| Flag / context | Mode | Who uses it |
|---|---|---|
| `--commit` | Commit | pre-commit hook |
| _(default)_ | Build | local `cargo mock`, CI |
| `--strict` | Push | pre-push hook |

Set per-gate severity in `mock/mockspace.toml`:

```toml
[lints.no-todo]
commit = "off"
build = "warn"
push = "error"
```

## Built-in lints active today

These are always available; severity is tuned per repo in
`mockspace.toml`.

| Lint | Purpose | Applicability today |
|---|---|---|
| `no-empty-crate` | Crate has no `pub` items | N/A while `mock/crates/` is empty — lint skips |
| `no-todo` | `todo!()` in source | Active once crates exist |
| `file-size` | File exceeds `max_lines` | Active once crates exist; cap = 400 |
| `undocumented-type` | Source type missing from design docs | Active once crates exist |
| `changelist-required` | Source changes without `src` changelist | Always on |
| `changelist-doc-gate` | Doc edits without `doc` changelist | Always on |
| `changelist-lock` | Edits to locked changelist | Always on |
| `changelist-immutability` | Edits to deprecated or frozen changelist | Always on |

The four `changelist-*` lints are built into mockspace and
non-negotiable — they enforce the design-round state machine.

## Post-R1–R4 lint roadmap

Once the compiler crate split lands (expected crates: `clause-lex`,
`clause-syntax`, `clause-resolve`, `clause-typecheck`, `clause-schedule`,
`clause-codegen`, `clause` orchestrator), the following categories of
lint will be authored:

| Lint (planned) | Preset | What it catches | Fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| `no-unsafe` | HARD_ERROR | `unsafe` block or fn in any compiler crate | Use safe abstraction; runtime C ABI is the only `unsafe` boundary and lives in the runtime repo |
| `no-dyn` | HARD_ERROR | `dyn Trait` / `TypeId` / `std::any::*` in framework code | Tagged enum or monomorphised trait dispatch |
| `strict-posture` | HARD_ERROR | Crate root missing `#![deny(unused, unreachable_code, unused_must_use, unused_imports, dead_code)]` | Add the deny attribute |
| `no-unwrap` | BUILD_GATE | `.unwrap()` / `.expect()` outside `#[cfg(test)]` | Propagate with `?`; invariant unwraps need `// invariant:` comment |
| `no-game-vocabulary` | BUILD_GATE | `clausewitz`, `witcher`, `stellaris`, `paradox`, `ck3`, `hoi4`, `eu4`, `the_sims`, `cities_skylines` in source or tests | Move the feature to an extension repo |
| `no-substrate-reimpl` | BUILD_GATE | Local graph / DAG / bitmask / sparse types shadowing `arvo` | Consume the substrate |
| `compiler-phase-layering` | HARD_ERROR | Upward or skipping imports between phases (lex → syntax → resolve → typecheck → codegen) | Respect the DAG; extract shared contracts to a lower crate |

Most of the compiler-phase layering lands as `[lints.forbidden-imports]`
rules in `mockspace.toml` rather than hand-authored `mock/lints/*.rs`
files. Rule skeleton:

```toml
[lints.forbidden-imports]
commit = "warn"
build = "error"
push = "error"
rules = [
    { scope = "{prefix}-lex",       forbidden = "{prefix}-syntax, {prefix}-resolve, {prefix}-typecheck, {prefix}-codegen, {prefix}-schedule", reason = "lex sits at the bottom of the compiler DAG" },
    { scope = "{prefix}-syntax",    forbidden = "{prefix}-resolve, {prefix}-typecheck, {prefix}-codegen, {prefix}-schedule", reason = "syntax consumes lex only" },
    # … continue the ladder after R1–R4 finalises names
]
```

## Custom lint authoring (when the time comes)

Custom lints live in `mock/lints/<name>.rs`. Each file exports:

```rust
pub fn lint() -> Box<dyn mockspace_lint_rules::Lint> { … }        // per-crate
pub fn cross_lint() -> Box<dyn mockspace_lint_rules::CrossCrateLint> { … }  // cross-crate
```

Files ending in `_cross.rs` are treated as cross-crate. Bootstrap
discovers them and wires them into the generated proxy crate on the
next `cargo mock` run.

Reference pattern: `~/Dev/saalis/mock/lints/no_vec_in_signatures.rs`
— a simple line-by-line scan with per-crate exemption.

## Hook coverage today

Two built-in hooks are always generated:

- `check-byline.sh` — byline policy from `mock/agent/config.toml`.
- `mockspace-write-guard.sh` — blocks writes to `.claude/**`,
  `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, `.github/instructions/`,
  `.github/skills/`, `.github/hooks/` from outside `mock/`.

Two repo-specific hooks ship today as reminders (not blockers):

- `no-game-vocabulary-reminder.sh` — nudges when game-specific
  vocabulary appears in a Write/Edit, pointing at the extension-repo
  pattern.
- `no-python-port-literal-guard.sh` — reminds that the Python
  prototype is a parity oracle, not a line-by-line translation source,
  when Write/Edit target Rust files in the compiler tree.

Crate-specific hooks (block `unsafe`, block `dyn`, block `.unwrap()`)
wait for R1–R4. They will be added alongside the matching lints.

## Running lints

```bash
# Default (Build mode) — standalone run
cargo mock --lint-only

# Commit mode — pre-commit hook equivalent
cargo mock --lint-only --commit

# Push mode — pre-push hook equivalent
cargo mock --lint-only --strict

# Full pipeline (check + lint + docs + agent regen)
cargo mock
```

## No-exception policy

Once a lint is enabled at `error`, flagged code is fixed — not
suppressed. `#[allow(...)]` for mockspace-driven lints is not accepted
without a design-round note justifying the carve-out.
